From 55c9a95ec80b79ebe6efee85193374cc454d8137 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:09:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] sparc64: validate sun4u interrupt vectors before table
 lookup

build_irq() uses the hardware interrupt number plus inofixup to index
ivector_table without checking its size. Reject an out-of-range result
before forming the bucket pointer; an unsigned comparison also rejects
negative values.

Use nr_ivec rather than assuming a fixed encoding or increasing the
table size. The default table has 0xfff entries, so vector 0xfff itself
is already outside the allocation. The generic-IRQ conversion removed
an earlier ino > NUM_IVECS check; reject equality as well.

Fixes: e18e2a00efc8 ("[SPARC64]: Move over to GENERIC_HARDIRQS.")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
---
 arch/sparc/kernel/irq_64.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/sparc/kernel/irq_64.c b/arch/sparc/kernel/irq_64.c
index 4f480a8cb66a..3f1a5b82a09f 100644
--- a/arch/sparc/kernel/irq_64.c
+++ b/arch/sparc/kernel/irq_64.c
@@ -615,6 +615,10 @@ unsigned int build_irq(int inofixup, unsigned long iclr, unsigned long imap)
 	BUG_ON(tlb_type == hypervisor);
 
 	ino = (upa_readq(imap) & (IMAP_IGN | IMAP_INO)) + inofixup;
+	if ((unsigned int)ino >= nr_ivec) {
+		prom_printf("IRQ: interrupt vector %d is out of range.\n", ino);
+		prom_halt();
+	}
 	bucket = &ivector_table[ino];
 	irq = bucket_get_irq(__pa(bucket));
 	if (!irq) {
